; Tutorial_8_Ask_with_SQL.inix -- a question in SQL, the database's own language, and the same kind of question in plain words.

[about]
Title=8 - Ask with SQL
Intro=MusicTrail asked which genre's greatest albums go back furthest, in one line of SQL; the answer moved through like a table; the history of questions; a question in plain words to a model on this computer; and working safely.
Setup=DbDo is open on MusicTrail.
Homework=Ask RadioTrail how many stations each country has, most first.

[step]

Say=One want: an answer no single command gives: for each genre, how far back its greatest albums go. SQL, the database's own language, asks it in one line.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Alt plus Control plus D, D for DbDo, opens it or brings it forward.
Key=Alt+Control+D
Hear=DbDo
Hear=DbDo ready

[step]

Say=Control plus Q, Q for Query, opens a box for SQL.
Key=Control+Q
Hear=Query dialog
Hear=SQL: edit, multiline
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I type the question.
Key=select genre, min(year) as earliest, count(*) as albums from albums group by genre order by earliest
Hear=select genre, min year as earliest, count as albums from albums group by genre order by earliest
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus Enter runs it from inside the box, where Enter would start a new line.
Key=Control+Enter
Hear=Vocal Jazz, 1954, 10, Row 1 of 10
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Vocal Jazz goes back furthest. The answer is a table like any other. Control plus End.
Key=Control+End
Hear=Hip Hop, 1987, 10, Row 10 of 10
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=And Hip Hop, the youngest. Shift plus Q says the query in force.
Key=Shift+Q
Hear=query: select genre, min year as earliest, count star as albums from albums group by genre order by earliest
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=A planned misstep: a misspelled column. The database names the word it does not know, and the box keeps the query to fix.
Key=Control+Q
Hear=Query dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Escape. Alt plus Shift plus Q, Query History, lists the questions asked, to run one again.
Key=Alt+Shift+Q
Hear=Query History
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=SQL is not the only way to ask. Escape, then Shift plus F12, Chat about Table, sends the table with a question in plain words to the model on this computer.
Key=Shift+F12
Hear=Chat about Table dialog
Hear=Question: edit
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=I ask which Soul albums came out in the nineteen seventies.
Key=Which Soul albums came out in the 1970s?
Hear=Which Soul albums came out in the 1970s?

[step]

Say=Enter. The answer comes in words, from the same records, and with the model running on this computer, the records are not sent anywhere.
Key=Enter
Hear=Answer dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Escape. An answer from SQL is a table, so Alt plus X exports it and Alt plus Shift plus S describes its columns. A question asked often can be saved as a script, a dot s q l file beside the database, and run with Control plus Shift plus I, as BookTrail's were.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Before a query that changes data, Alt plus Z, Toggle Read Only, makes the database read only, so a mistyped statement cannot change anything.
Key=Alt+Z
Hear=Read only

[step]

Say=Alt plus Z again makes it writable when you mean to change it. After a change, F5 shows the table as it now stands.
Key=Alt+Z
Hear=Read and write

[step]

Say=Practise on a copy: Save As, Control plus Shift plus S, makes one, so the original stays as it was while you learn.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=What this walk taught. I name the command; the reader gives the key.
Key=
Hear=

[step]

Say=Ask in SQL.
Key=
Hear=Control plus Q

[step]

Say=Run it from inside the box.
Key=
Hear=Control plus Enter

[step]

Say=The questions asked before.
Key=
Hear=Alt plus Shift plus Q

[step]

Say=Ask in plain words.
Key=
Hear=Shift plus F12

[step]

Say=Make the database read only.
Key=
Hear=Alt plus Z
